/**
\fn double pdg::PhysicsConstraint::getMinAngle() const
\brief Read the rotary limit's minimum relative angle.
\return The lower bound for body B's rotation minus body A's, in radians, clockwise positive. Throws for other constraint types. A retained disconnected rotary limit remains queryable.
\see setAngleLimits(), Part::setIKLimits()
*/
/**
\fn double pdg::PhysicsConstraint::getMaxAngle() const
\brief Read the rotary limit's maximum relative angle.
\return The upper bound for body B's rotation minus body A's, in radians, clockwise positive. Throws for other constraint types. A retained disconnected rotary limit remains queryable.
\see setAngleLimits(), Part::setIKLimits()
*/
/**
\fn PhysicsConstraint& pdg::PhysicsConstraint::setAngleLimits(double minAngle, double maxAngle)
\brief Change both bounds of a rotary-limit constraint.

Both bounds must be finite and ordered; equal values lock the relative angle.
Invalid input leaves both old bounds intact. Other constraint types throw.
Getters and linked Part IK see the change immediately. Both physics solvers apply
it on the next constraint step. This does not teleport either body or reconnect
a disconnected constraint. The physical interval may span multiple turns;
Part IK links accept at most one turn and report an error for a wider interval.

\param minAngle Minimum body B rotation relative to A, in radians.
\param maxAngle Maximum body B rotation relative to A, in radians.
\return This constraint for chaining.
\see getMinAngle(), getMaxAngle(), Part::setIKLimits()
*/
